total of 45 pad-rows in every sector.

The gas gain is controlled by the anode wire voltage and is set independently for the inner and outer sectors to generate a signal to noise ratio of 20:1 for pads intercepting the centre of tracks that drifted the full half-length of the TPC.

The outer sub-sector has continuous pad coverage to optimise dE/dx resolution while the inner sub-sector (the region of highest track density) is optimised for good two-hit resolution with smaller pads (detailed discussion of optimisations can be found in [124, 131]).

Given the time of the collision, the read-out time and location, it is possible to reconstruct the 3D location of any ionisation event in the TPC. This allows the full 3D reconstruction of tracks in the TPC.

